# Everything here is read by FreeBSD: shell scripts, rc scripts, Python and
# configuration files. A CRLF checkout on Windows must not turn into a CRLF file
# on the firewall, where /bin/sh would read the carriage return as part of the
# command and an rc script would fail in a way nobody would guess from the error.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# The site (npuforge.org) and the problem reports' relay are services of their own, deployed from
# here by their own workflows; neither is installed on an appliance. Left out of every archive of a
# commit - the tarball an appliance's update downloads, and an image's - so an update carries the
# driver and its plugin and nothing of the site's (2026-10-22).
website/ export-ignore
relay/ export-ignore
